# qqcandy: staged CCIF bring-up diagnostic. Phase A enables six real
# infra-ao clock gates and reads the AP CCIF bank; phase B reads the MD
# bank; phase C initializes the CCISM ring buffers (the first write to
# modem-visible memory, safe while the modem is held in reset) and
# registers the CCIF IRQs masked. Module-only keeps all of it out of the
# boot image, but does not isolate hardware faults.

config MTK_CCCI_CCIF
	tristate "MediaTek CCI CCIF staged bring-up diagnostic (loadable module)"
	depends on ARCH_MEDIATEK && MTK_EMBED_BOARD_DTB && MTK_CCCI_UTIL
	depends on m
	default n
	help
	  Staged, opt-in diagnostics for the MT6895 CCIF hardware interface.
	  Loading maps nothing. Three one-shot triggers (0600) must run in
	  order: ccif_clk enables the six official CCIF clock gates (set
	  registers only, latch-verified, restored on unload) and reads the
	  AP CCIF bank; ccif_md reads the MD bank; ccif_ring parses the LK
	  tags fresh, initializes the 16 normal + 16 exception ring buffers
	  inside CCISM_MCU/CCISM_MCU_EXP with the official layout, and
	  registers the two CCIF IRQs with IRQF_NO_AUTOEN (masked; the
	  handler cannot run until a later explicit enable).

	  Even so, none of this isolates a bus fault; a wrong gate write or
	  region could still hang the SoC.
